This repository carries two licenses, because the two kinds of content carry
different constraints. Neither file supersedes the other; each governs the
directories named below.

  code/                                    MIT              see LICENSE-code
  sample_qa/  eval_questions/  verdicts/   CC BY-NC 4.0     see LICENSE-data

The sessions behind the released samples come from service data where speakers
consented to research and non-commercial use. The non-commercial term on the
data follows that consent. It is not an open-source license and not an open-data
license, and we do not describe it as one.

The analysis code carries no such constraint and is MIT.

